Phasmid: Windows text metrics (Windows profiles)

What:     A windows profile measures text as Windows Chrome does through
          DirectWrite: OS/2 win (or typo, with USE_TYPO_METRICS) ascent and
          descent without VDMX or descent borrow, the GDI line gap, the
          advance of 'x' as the average character width, linear advances
          with subpixel positioning at every scale factor, integer
          GDI-classic advances (hdmx, else the bitmap strike's, else
          rounded) for faces with an EBLC strike at the GDI ppem, and
          synthetic bold from weight 600. Linux profiles are unchanged.
Why:      The Linux scaler gives the same Windows font files Linux vertical
          metrics, line heights and widths.
Profile:  os.family
Hooks:    third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_metrics.cc
          AscentDescentWithHacks; simple_font_data.cc PlatformInit,
          WidthForGlyph; font_platform_data.cc CreateSkFont;
          shaping/harfbuzz_font_data.h UpdateFallbackMetricsAndScale;
          shaping/harfbuzz_face.cc HarfBuzzGetGlyphHorizontalAdvance(s);
          skia/font_cache_skia.cc CreateFontPlatformData; new
          fonts/windows_text_metrics.{h,cc}; platform BUILD.gn
Contexts: main, iframes, dedicated, shared and service workers,
          OffscreenCanvas; headless and headful.
Guard:    tests/guards/fonts/windows_metrics.py

